@startuml
title Testcontainers example: one lifecycle per worker JVM
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #2563EB
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFBEB
skinparam noteBorderColor #D97706
hide footbox

participant "Executing test classes\nin one Gradle worker" as tests
participant "TestInfrastructure\nlazy static holder" as fixture
database "Worker-local\nPostgreSQL" as postgres
queue "Worker-local\nRabbitMQ" as rabbit

note over tests,rabbit
  ShardPilot has already filtered candidate classes.
  Each other shard / worker has its own independent fixture pair.
end note

tests -> fixture : First class: prepare database
group Initialize holder once; Startables.deepStart(...).join()
  par Start PostgreSQL
    fixture -> postgres : Start with random mapped port
    postgres --> fixture : Ready; JDBC endpoint
  else Start RabbitMQ
    fixture -> rabbit : Start with random mapped ports
    rabbit --> fixture : Ready; AMQP endpoint
  end
end
fixture -> postgres : CREATE DATABASE example_<generated A>
fixture --> tests : Class A JDBC URL
tests -> postgres : JDBC assertions; close connections
tests -> rabbit : Private queue; AMQP assertions; close clients

tests -> fixture : Next class: prepare database
fixture -> postgres : CREATE DATABASE example_<generated B>
fixture --> tests : Class B JDBC URL; same live container pair
tests -> postgres : Independent class data
tests -> rabbit : New exclusive queues / connections

note over tests,rabbit
  Nested tests stay with their outer class and database.
  No per-class container stop; no @Container extension ownership.
end note

tests -> tests : Worker exits after its selected tests
note over postgres,rabbit
  Testcontainers Ryuk removes the disposable containers.
  No cross-run reusable containers or external application services.
end note
@enduml
